This aircraft is a JSBSim model of NASA's six-seat Quadrotor, one of NASA's reference vehicles for Urban Air
Mobility, in its turboshaft version (Quad TS) with collective control and flapping rotors. PteroLabs wrote it in 2026
and named it Stork; its meshes are built from NASA's OpenVSP model. NASA does not endorse PteroSim.

The flight model (stork.xml, the files it assembles, Engines/ and Systems/) is PteroLabs' work, distributed under
the GNU General Public License v3.0; see LICENSE in this folder for its text. Its numbers come from:

  Silva, Johnson, Antcliff and Patterson, AIAA 2018-3847, Table 3, column Quad TS: design gross weight, empty
  weight, payload, fuel tank, rotor radius, tip speed, solidity, drag areas, engine power, and the hover, cruise and
  maximum speed performance the model is checked against.

  Johnson, Silva and Solis, "Concept Vehicles for VTOL Air Taxi Operations", AHS 2018 (NTRS 20180003381): the
  rotor design, its twist and pitch-flap coupling.
    https://ntrs.nasa.gov/citations/20180003381

  NASA's NDARC input files for the concept (quadrotor6.list, quadrotor6.run, gen500.list): blade count, lift-curve
  slope, flap frequency, Lock number, tip loss, hub and landing gear drag, fixed useful load, passenger weight,
  rotation senses, and the GEN500 engine's ratings, lapse and fuel flow.

  Johnson, NDARC theory, NASA/TP-2015-218751: hinge offset and blade inertia from the flap frequency and Lock
  number, engine scaling and lapse, fuel flow at part power, the one-engine-inoperative rating.

  NASA's OpenVSP model of the Quadrotor (meshes/NOTICE): all geometry, the rotor and skid positions, the mass parts
  behind the centre of gravity and the inertia, the fuel tank.

Chosen, with no source, and marked so where they appear: the skid springs, damping and friction, the collective's
upper stop, the transmission inertia, the shaft governor's gains and engage point, the airframe drag area being the
same in every direction, and the engines' N1, ITT and start values, which are template values as on Orca.
README.md lists the model's known limits.

The ArduPilot parameter file (firmwares/ardupilot_stork.param) sets ArduPilot parameters to PteroLabs' values for
this vehicle. ArduPilot is distributed under the GNU General Public License v3.0.
